                     color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Iran Vows ‘Devastating’ Response as U.S. Threatens Toughest Sanctions\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Iran has warned that any fresh economic offensive by the United States would trigger a ‘devastating’ response. The warning came on Friday after US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the administration would unveil details of its planned sanctions on Monday. The confrontation is also weighing on global oil markets, with crude prices heading for a second consecutive weekly gain.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/iran-vows-devastating-response-as-us-threatens-toughest-sanctions\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Atiku Proposes Targeted Refinery Subsidy Under 2027 Economic Plan\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Former Vice President Atiku Abubakar has proposed replacing Nigeria’s former petrol import subsidy with a targeted production-support programme for local refineries if he wins the 2027 presidential election. Atiku said the plan was designed to reduce energy costs while expanding domestic refining.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/atiku-proposes-targeted-refinery-subsidy-under-2027-economic-plan\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Kenya, Ethiopia and Rwanda Eye 30% Stake in Dangote’s $17bn East Africa Refinery\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Kenya, Ethiopia and Rwanda have expressed interest in taking equity positions in Dangote Industries’ proposed refinery project in Kenya. Nigerian industrialist offering East African countries a combined 30% stake in the planned $17 billion facility. Kenya is considering a 10% interest valued at approximately $500 million.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/kenya-ethiopia-and-rwanda-eye-30-stake-in-dangotes-17bn-east-africa-refinery\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Climb for Second Week as Iran Crisis Raises Supply Risks\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude stood at $93.39 per barrel, down 0.42 per cent, while West Texas Intermediate (WTI) traded at $86.32 per barrel. The modest daily declines have not erased the broader weekly gains, with geopolitical risks continuing to provide support for prices.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-climb-for-second-week-as-iran-crisis-raises-supply-risks\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
